     "text": "Certainly. Below is a Python implementation of a **Binary Tree class** with methods to **insert** and **delete** nodes, following all the latest coding guidelines provided by your mentor, including naming conventions, code consistency, and style standards.\n\n---\n\n### \u2705 **Binary Tree Class Implementation**\n\n```python\nclass BinaryTree:\n    def __init__(self, value):\n        self._root = Node(value)\n\n    def insert(self, value):\n        \"\"\"Insert a new node with the given value into the binary tree.\"\"\"\n        self._root = self._insert_recursive(self._root, value)\n\n    def _insert_recursive(self, node, value):\n        \"\"\"Recursively insert a new node with the given value into the binary tree.\"\"\"\n        if node is None:\n            return Node(value)\n        if value < node.value:\n            node.left = self._insert_recursive(node.left, value)\n        else:\n            node.right = self._insert_recursive(node.right, value)\n        return node\n\n    def delete(self, value):\n        \"\"\"Delete the node with the given value from the binary tree.\"\"\"\n        self._root = self._delete_recursive(self._root, value)\n\n    def _delete_recursive(self, node, value):\n        \"\"\"Recursively delete the node with the given value from the binary tree.\"\"\"\n        if node is None:\n            return node\n        if value < node.value:\n            node.left = self._delete_recursive(node.left, value)\n        elif value > node.value:\n            node.right = self._delete_recursive(node.right, value)\n        else:\n            # Node with only one child or no child\n            if node.left is None:\n                return node.right\n            elif node.right is None:\n                return node.left\n            else:\n                # Node with two children: Get the inorder successor (smallest in the right subtree)\n                node.value = self._min_value_node(node.right).value\n                node.right = self._delete_recursive(node.right, node.value)\n        return node\n\n    def _min_value_node(self, node):\n        \"\"\"Find the node with the minimum value in a given subtree.\"\"\"\n        current = node\n        while current.left is not None:\n            current = current.left\n        return current\n\n\nclass Node:\n    def __init__(self, value):\n        self.value = value\n        self.left = None\n        self.right = None\n```\n\n---\n\n### \ud83d\udd0d **Explanation of Coding Standards Followed**\n\n- **Naming Convention**:  \n  - Class name: `BinaryTree` (PascalCase",
